###
# Test-harness and local state.
#
# The deep patterns are deliberate: podman (buildah 4.9.3) matches a pattern **without a slash only
# against the context root**, unlike gitignore, which matches such a name at any depth. Verified by
# building a scratch context whose `.dockerignore` held the bare name `.vscode-test` and watching the
# nested `ext/rest-fs/.vscode-test` arrive in the image anyway. These entries used to be written the
# gitignore way, so `ext/rest-fs/.vscode-test` (fifteen downloaded VS Code builds, ~15 GB), every
# package's `node_modules` (~9 GB), `.tap` (~2 GB) and `coverage` (~2 GB) all reached the builder: a
# ~28 GB context, a 26 GB builder image per build, and a dangling image of that size left behind each
# time (F-379, which the earlier fix did not actually cure; measured again as F-406).
**/node_modules
**/.vscode-test
**/tap-snapshots
**/.tap
**/allure-results*
**/allure-report
**/rush-logs
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
